## Type Safety / Validasi (5 temuan)

### T1. `@Req() req: any` — 90+ untyped request objects

Semua controller pakai `req: any`. Artinya `req.user`, `req.cookies`, `req.headers` semua tanpa type checking.

**Fix konkret:** Buat interface:
```typescript
// shared/core/interfaces/authenticated-request.interface.ts
import { Request } from 'express';

interface JwtPayload {
  id: string;        // ← standardize dari K2
  email: string;
  role: UserRole;
}

export interface AuthenticatedRequest extends Request {
  user: JwtPayload;
}
```

Replace semua `req: any` → `req: AuthenticatedRequest`. Ini juga **fix K2** sekaligus — begitu tipe jelas, fallback `id || userId` jadi compile error.

**Effort: 2 jam. Benefit: HIGH** — fix K2 + T1 sekaligus, prevent future bugs.

---

### T2. `catch (error: any)` — 16 occurrences

File: `zoom-booking.service.ts` (4×), `zoom-api.adapter.ts` (3×), `zoom-booking.controller.ts`, `webapp.service.ts`, `telegram.module.ts`, `pdf-ocr.service.ts`, `push-channel.service.ts`, `eform-notification.listener.ts` (4×).

TypeScript 4.4+ default `catch` variable = `unknown`. `error: any` explicitly opt-out type safety.

**Fix:** Ganti `catch (error: any)` → `catch (error)` atau `catch (error: unknown)`, lalu narrow:
```typescript
catch (error: unknown) {
  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);
  this.logger.error(message);
}
```

**Effort: 1 jam.** Mostly mechanical.

