### T4. `Record<string, any>` di 40+ entity/DTO columns

Dipakai untuk JSONB columns: audit logs, preferences, form data, meeting settings, custom fields.

**Contoh paling berisiko:**
| File | Field | Risk |
|------|-------|------|
| [notification.controller.ts:96](file:///d:/iDesk-main/apps/backend/src/modules/notifications/notification.controller.ts#L96) | `@Body() updates: Record<string, any>` | Client kirim apapun langsung ke DB |
| [access-request.entity.ts:50](file:///d:/iDesk-main/apps/backend/src/modules/access-request/entities/access-request.entity.ts#L50) | `customFormData: Record<string, any>` | Unvalidated user input stored |
| [zoom-meeting.entity.ts:36](file:///d:/iDesk-main/apps/backend/src/modules/zoom-booking/entities/zoom-meeting.entity.ts#L36) | `meetingSettings: Record<string, any>` | External API response stored raw |

**Fix pragmatis:** Untuk **entity columns** yang store external data (audit, API response) → `Record<string, any>` acceptable. Untuk **`@Body()` parameters** → wajib ganti ke typed DTO. Prioritas: `notification.controller.ts` lines 96 + 103.

